  "audio_budget_guard": {
    "_note": "Chosen by Sinin, 2026-09-30, instead of cutting Pro to 12 voices or 3 slots. dsp_limits stay as they are. Before each block the DSP sums the measured cost of the active modules; if the total would exceed max_block_share of the block (budgeted per second, so it holds at 96 kHz too), it downgrades, then bypasses, the heaviest voice slots first, lowest-weighted families first, until it fits. Per-module costs come from the DSP thread's measurements (measured_dsp). Applies to every tier; measured today it only engages in Pro worst cases and at 96 kHz in Standard and Pro.",
